  "id": "hot-plate",
  "term": "hot plate",
  "definition": "A hot plate is a laboratory pain test in which an animal is placed on a heated surface, such as one set to 52 or 56 degrees, to measure pain-stimulated responses and the effects of drugs on acute pain. In this source, the hot plate test is used as an assay of antinociception.",
